## ⚡ Quickstart

> Runs on Jetson AGX Thor (JetPack 7.x, `sm_110`) and Jetson Orin (JetPack 7.2.1+, `sm_87`) with Docker + the NVIDIA Container Toolkit — the kernel family resolves from the device at runtime.

```bash
docker pull {{ ctx.image }}

# any model, any vLLM flags — Mjolnir serves the decode:
docker run --rm -it --gpus all --ipc host -p 8000:8000 -e VLLM_KV_CACHE_LAYOUT=HND \
  {{ ctx.image }} <model> --kv-cache-dtype fp8 --attention-backend MJOLNIR
```

The recommended path is the **mjolnir CLI** ([`mjolnir-cli`](https://pypi.org/project/mjolnir-cli/) on PyPI) on the host: `uv tool install mjolnir-cli && mjolnir serve up` manages this image and serves the model from a YAML config — and `mjolnir bench` / `mjolnir verify` reproduce every number in the [case study](https://github.com/thor-arena/mjolnir/blob/main/docs/platforms/thor/README.md).

## ⚡ Tags

Tags follow the **upstream vLLM version** of the base image, not the kernel's:

- `v{{ ctx.vllm_version }}` — the current image (re-pushed on every rebuild)
- `v{{ ctx.vllm_version }}-<sha>` — the same build, immutable per commit
- `latest` — moved by each release

A kernel release is rebuilt into the same `v{{ ctx.vllm_version }}` tag; the kernel version rides along as the `io.github.thor-arena.mjolnir.kernel-version` image label.

